body:
AVI-SPL's Support and Maintenance page sets out the AV/UC support options available once rooms are in use, including a 24/7 help desk and field dispatch. AVI-SPL offers both on-site resources and remote technical support, delivered through a global network of distributed technicians who know local conditions and methods.

**What to know**

Service level agreements come in several tiers, with add-on "plus" options to tailor them. Support options include:
- manufacturer warranty support;
- a help desk with unlimited use, open 24/7 every day;
- repair and service dispatch locally.

**Enhanced support** (extra remote responsiveness):
- remote help desk support without limit, 24/7 every day, globally;
- help with manufacturer warranty repair or replacement programs, which AVI-SPL facilitates;
- software and firmware updates applied remotely to covered assets.

**Elite support** (extra onsite responsiveness):
- onsite support without limit, M-F, 8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m. local time;
- unlimited global remote help desk support, 24/7;
- the same facilitation of manufacturer warranty repair or replacement programs;
- the same remote software and firmware updates for covered assets.

**Enterprise Maintenance** is a subscription service providing 24/7 technical support for audio-visual and unified collaboration spaces, intended to simplify management and reduce cost of ownership. It includes:
- certified technicians providing support 24/7;
- coverage of over 700 manufacturer technologies;
- a fixed price subscription, whatever technology is deployed;
- in-room technology changes supported automatically;
- portability of the service to new rooms/room locations;
- flexible subscription options, for remote support or on-site support;
- room subscriptions sized at 25, 100, and 250 rooms;
- 1 and 3-year term options.

**How to reach support**: the page refers to the AVI-SPL Help Desk portal, which requires a customer login.

**Customer comment on the page**: a verified user, a Manager in Information Technology at a construction company with 10,001+ employees, calls AVI-SPL their preferred AV vendor and says AVI-SPL helped convert all conference rooms larger than 10 people to Teams, and that these are now the most used conference rooms on campus.

**When to use this**: questions about which support tier includes onsite visits, help desk hours, what Enterprise Maintenance covers, or the subscription sizes and terms.

**Not stated in this source**: prices, response or resolution time targets, and a help desk phone number.
